  "video_id": "JQ_u7V3zXLw",
  "title": "Someone Open Sourced An Entire AI Company",
  "description": "A free MIT-licensed repo with 135,338 stars holds 279 specialist AI agents sorted into 19 departments: marketing, sales, support, finance, paid media, project management and more. Each agent is a plain markdown file that gives your AI a role, a working method and an output format, so instead of one assistant that half-knows everything you get a proposal writer, a support responder, a pipeline analyst and a bookkeeper.\n\nThey run inside Claude Code with their own context windows and report back a finished draft. Installing them grants no new access, since they are only instruction files.\n\nGet the exact install commands for Windows and Mac, the 12 worth installing if you run a business, and a build-your-own template with three filled examples: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J3mahlxALfhfnPk1dxeWBbdCs3Uc-_A14SxVU__7xk/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #AIAgents #ClaudeAI",
